  "paper_id": "https://openalex.org/W2962785754",
  "title": "HIBERT: Document Level Pre-training of Hierarchical Bidirectional Transformers for Document Summarization",
  "abstract": "Neural extractive summarization models usually employ a hierarchical encoder for document encoding and they are trained using sentence-level labels, which are created heuristically using rule-based methods. Training the hierarchical encoder with these inaccurate labels is challenging. Inspired by the recent work on pre-training transformer sentence encoders We apply the pre-trained HIBERT to our summarization model and it outperforms its randomly initialized counterpart by 1.25 ROUGE on the CNN/Dailymail dataset and by 2.0 ROUGE on a version of New York Times dataset. We also achieve the state-of-the-art performance on these two datasets.",
